: \"56d3e167bd5ec90e5a1023d4460aead53b334d091f14ff2c8d02259d721483bb\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1_step_live_rng_0_1.json\", \"sha256\": \"a0e4a6230e296b1447ada549bb9c4fb429c58cc45a7861c5e9e7b039e2d0bef6\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1_step_detach_rng_0_1.json\", \"sha256\": \"0cdcf8ef4fc70264c5c8d8e551efcbacf2698e3b3e032faa5f7f36b43cf2a3f7\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-N2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"No training with oracle object IDs or validation-tuned language/mask grouping. Same-object selection inconsistency exists, but label-free nearest-language precision is 121/441 and overlapping-mask grouping is 171/354. Reconsider only on a prospectively justified inference-valid relation mechanism.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1-N3_diagnosis_20260926-183100.md\", \"sha256\": \"f4b71e7e2485a3281acbb15eea2d6802a2f39b4712eb65200fcbd3b3c0514cc9\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N2_language_proxy_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"1290b06e9ce4956a96e9723456f596f1bacc2603ba0a726ae56cf9379828335c\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N2_scene_consensus_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"afc9adb429aad8cb455ed87f5678df04af0f7442c8ff861eb59acaee2c962f21\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-N3\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not implement collision-only exclusivity loss. Native B4 yielded just 6/365 distinct-target pair collisions in 64 training scenes; reconsider only with independent evidence of a substantially different cross-expression confidence mechanism, not a loss-weight scan.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N1-N3_diagnosis_20260926-183100.md\", \"sha256\": \"f4b71e7e2485a3281acbb15eea2d6802a2f39b4712eb65200fcbd3b3c0514cc9\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-N3_collisions_64scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"562e2139756a4338b47ad6a4281db24e26ac1f94ee3d361ebeae5645ff3c52ba\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-O1\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not admit token-masking confidence. Inference counterfactual changes expression semantics and reduced overall mIoU on train and validation; no matched semantic-preserving control. Reconsider only with a prospectively specified meaning-preserving intervention and native paired training diagnosis, not a token-position or fusion scan.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_o1_language_perturbation.py\", \"sha256\": \"ab26198f6b41e56536bd69b2a539212789cd1ad87158fa43894e6fd9e365e700\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1_language_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"cc36895197a8142d4a09a7f2f58d1116d260bea635fe64db647291d3d1bbfc3d\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1_language_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"a730f74c62907022a1161f0e0f9714b3103869168639e2990dfaefd68dac8db5\"}\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AdaRES-O2\",\n      \"stage\": \"rejected\",\n      \"next_action\": \"Do not admit whole-appearance removal or a learned confidence gate derived from it. Removing all 2D features causes general distribution shift rather than error-specific evidence (422/455 query flips, mIoU 0.831 to 0.286). Reconsider only with independently justified localized modality evidence and a matched native control.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"path\": \"AdaRES/tools/diagnose_adares_o2_appearance_counterfactual.py\", \"sha256\": \"8db494c678768cf43bfa598ba980f2e56dfa303a745a812512097999919c3065\"},\n        {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O2_appearance_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"f1ee25ea70d463d306215f038ac8e2105c182b27b6f2555883fc8ed3adc3f42b\"}\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"design_cycle\": {\n    \"at\": \"2026-09-26T19:02:00+08:00\",\n    \"candidate_budget\": 2,\n    \"admitted\": 0,\n    \"attempted_ids\": [\"AdaRES-O1\", \"AdaRES-O2\"],\n    \"stop_reason\": \"independent_routes_exhausted\",\n    \"stop_detail\": \"Two distinct executable routes failed native diagnosis/control: O1 token masking perturbed expression semantics and reduced overall train/val quality; O2 global 2D feature removal collapsed both correct and erroneous predictions. No other independent evidence-backed executable route was identified in this bounded review. No global scientific exhaustion is claimed.\",\n    \"evidence\": [\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1_language_16scenes_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"cc36895197a8142d4a09a7f2f58d1116d260bea635fe64db647291d3d1bbfc3d\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1_language_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"a730f74c62907022a1161f0e0f9714b3103869168639e2990dfaefd68dac8db5\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O2_appearance_train16_20260926.json\", \"sha256\": \"f1ee25ea70d463d306215f038ac8e2105c182b27b6f2555883fc8ed3adc3f42b\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1-O2_diagnosis_20260926-190200.md\", \"sha256\": \"6ae221f02c0bbe7f6411e7f97411887bacacc233d2f5918b111d4f0e993c5cc8\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-190200.md\", \"sha256\": \"9ecca475bfc2f873fa995bcfaf10f0b47057db89a01f7004426f2c3c4a9610cf\"},\n      {\"path\": \"pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-190200.md\", \"sha256\": \"2b64089458f5c310375d2ca7e6067df18fc5e8ef5243883c0dadb0adadfb0e70\"}\n    ],\n    \"resume_condition\": \"Next capacity-gap tick: identify independently justified inference-available metric-aligned confidence evidence beyond O1/O2 and earlier rejected routes; freeze a semantic-preserving paired control and native batch test before all six admission gates. Reconcile any monitor/goal event first.\"\n  },\n  \"migration_notes\": \"AdaRES did not previously have research work tracking; B4 and B5 are the first explicit queued records.\"\n}\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/goal.json'\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"metric\": {\n    \"name\": \"mIoU\",\n    \"target\": 0.515,\n    \"dataset\": \"ScanRefer\"\n  },\n  \"baseline_experiment_id\": \"AdaRES-B1\",\n  \"description\": \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\",\n  \"constraints\": [\n    \"Use server-2 GPUs 0 and 1 only; never use server-6.\",\n    \"All experiments launched after AdaRES-B3 must use exactly one GPU; run at most one independent experiment on GPU 0 and one on GPU 1.\",\n    \"Do not design or queue a successor while AdaRES-B3 is running; after B3 reaches a terminal state, admit at most two structurally independent single-GPU candidates.\",\n    \"Use a fixed 30-epoch protocol for the B2 and B4 extension. Resume both from their epoch-20 last checkpoints without resetting the optimizer or LR scheduler; do not tune the epoch count on validation.\",\n    \"Train from the released SPFormer sparse-UNet backbone; the decoder is authored in this project.\",\n    \"Report mIoU, Acc@0.25, Acc@0.5, active queries, latency, and peak memory.\",\n    \"Do not tune thresholds, temperatures, loss weights, feature subsets, or the fixed 30-epoch protocol on ScanRefer validation.\"\n  ],\n  \"banned\": [\n    \"Do not use server-6.\",\n    \"Do not report the released b005/CFNet checkpoints as AdaRES-B0 results.\",\n    \"Do not scan the ranking margin or the occupancy loss weight on validation.\"\n  ],\n  \"pipeline_policy\": {\n    \"research_on_capacity_gap\": true,\n    \"steady_ticks_before_design\": 1,\n    \"fill_to_capacity\": true,\n    \"design_buffer\": 0,\n    \"max_candidates_per_design_tick\": 2\n  }\n}\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/analyses/AdaRES-O1-O2_diagnosis_20260926-190200.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# Native diagnostic cycle: O1 and O2\n\n2026-09-26 19:02 Asia/Shanghai. Prepared monitor and goal preflight used once; no training or queue mutation. Native B4-E30 best checkpoint, server-2 GPU0. Inference probes only; no loss backward or admission resource profile.\n\n## O1: Language counterfactual selection\nFixed first/last content-token masking, with unchanged-input repeat control. On 16 validation scenes (441 expressions), repeat mismatch 0, 240 material selection errors. First-token selection flipped in 179/240 errors and 105/201 other expressions; last-token in 169/240 and 100/201. Whole-cohort selected mIoU: baseline 0.49186, first 0.48429, last 0.49538. On 16 separate training scenes (455 expressions), repeat mismatch 0, 107 material errors; first flipped 66/107 errors and 218/348 others, last 66/107 and 193/348. Training selected mIoU fell from 0.83083 to 0.80476/0.81930. The apparent error association is confounded: masking a content token can change referent semantics, and both interventions harm overall training quality. This is not a matched semantic-preserving confidence control. Reject O1; no token-position or fusion scan on validation.\n\n## O2: Global 2D appearance removal\nOn the fixed first 16 training scenes, repeat mismatch 0. Zeroing all 2D features flipped 101/107 material errors and 321/348 other expressions; selected-mask overlap was 0.344 versus 0.315, respectively. Selected mIoU fell from 0.83083 to 0.28600. Global feature removal is a broad out-of-distribution perturbation without error-specific direction; it does not isolate confidence in a particular query. Reject O2 without spending validation samples on a feature-removal scan.\n\n## Gates and limitations\nBoth probes were deterministic and ran with peak reserved GPU memory 4.01 GiB (O1 validation), 3.46 GiB (O1 training and O2 training). These are inference-only bounded measurements, not native backward execution, training resources or worst-case memory. Diagnosis and matched-control gates fail; implementation, admission receipt, sync and dispatch are unauthorized. O1 first validation cohort matches the previously fixed 16-scene diagnostic subset, so no numerical intervention may be selected from it. No full literature novelty or theoretical derivation claim. A future independent mechanism needs a frozen paired native control and all six gates before admission.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/reviews/motivation_review_20260926-190200.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# Motivation Review - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 19:02 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Goal\nAdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515. B1 0.5020; B4-E30 0.5094; gap 0.0056. Constraints: server-2 GPUs 0/1 only, one independent task per GPU, released backbone and project decoder, fixed B2/B4 continuation, report mIoU/Acc@0.25/Acc@0.5/active queries/latency/peak memory, no validation tuning of thresholds/temperatures/weights/features/epochs. Bans: no server-6, no released checkpoint as B0, no margin/occupancy-weight scan.\n\n## 2. Story Status\n| Hypothesis | Status | Evidence | Gap |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Competition-aware confidence | Partial | B4-E30 0.5094 | Below target, no fresh matched control |\n| Metric-IoU targets | Negative | G1 0.4980 | Do not tune targets |\n| Language perturbation stability | Confounded | O1 train and validation selected mIoU decline | Semantic-preserving paired control |\n| Appearance counterfactual | Negative | O2 train mIoU 0.831 to 0.286 | Localized evidence rather than global shift |\n\n## 3. Experiment Assessment\nB1 0.5020, B4-E30 0.5094, D1 0.5080, F4 0.5060, H5 0.5061, G1 0.4980. None reaches 0.515. Prior N1/N2/N3 and earlier negative diagnoses remain closed under their specific evidence. O1/O2 are diagnostic probes, not trained experiments.\n\n## 4. Gap Analysis\nThe fixed B4 cohort has large oracle-selection headroom, but the oracle label is unavailable at inference. A confidence mechanism must isolate query quality without changing the expression or destroying a complete modality. Native backward, matched training controls, active-query/latency and training memory measurements are absent for O1/O2.\n\n## 5. Design Rationale\nO1 tested whether language evidence dependence distinguishes incorrect selection, using fixed content-token interventions and repeat control on training and validation scenes. O2 separately tested whether 2D appearance dependence distinguishes errors, using zero-input intervention and repeat control on training scenes. The diagnoses do not justify a trainable confidence mechanism; a token-position, feature-subset, or fusion-weight scan would violate the goal and smell check.\n\n## 6. Next Batch\nNo admission. See `pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-190200.md`; future independently justified route must pass all six gates.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\chuanle song\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Microsoft\\\\WindowsApps\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content -Raw 'pipeline/designs/exp_design_20260926-190200.md'\"","aggregated_output":"# Experiment Design - AdaRES_project\n\n2026-09-26 19:02 Asia/Shanghai\n\n## 1. Motivation\nGoal: \"AdaRES: improve a faithful standard-indicator 3D referring expression segmentation baseline by learning query confidence from metric-aligned evidence, targeting ScanRefer mIoU >= 0.515.\" Capacity gap 2/2, candidate budget 2. O1/O2 tested whether inference-available counterfactual evidence could expose the selection gap without oracle labels.\n\n## 2. Current Best Results\n| ID | State | mIoU | Acc@0.25 | Acc@0.5 | spmIoU |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| B1 | complete | 0.5020 | 0.610 | 0.553 | 0.467 |\n| B4-E30 | champion | 0.5094 | 0.608 | 0.562 | 0.474 |\n| H5 | early stop | 0.5061 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n| G1 | complete | 0.4980 | unavailable | unavailable | unavailable |\n\n## 3. Analysis & Direction\nO1 fixed token masking changes expression semantics, with train mIoU 0.83083 to 0.80476/0.81930 and validation 0.49186 to 0.48429/0.49538. O2 global 2D removal induces broad model failure, train mIoU 0.83083 to 0.28600. Neither is task-specific, metric-aligned evidence for a new query confidence path.\n\n## 4. Experiment Plan\nNo candidate admitted. O1 fails semantic-preserving matched controls; O2 fails specificity and matched controls. Neither has native backward execution for a structural implementation. No model/config, receipt or queue entry is authorized. Distinct future hypotheses must have a frozen native matched intervention, backward, resources, independence and constraints checks.\n\n## 5. GPU Allocation Plan\nServer-2 GPU0 and GPU1 remain unassigned by this project's queue after GPU0 inference probes completed. Server-6 excluded. No live occupancy conclusion beyond the targeted idle GPU query before probes.\n\n## 6. Implementation Checklist\n- [x] Native fixed-cohort O1 val and train readouts with repeat control.\n- [x] Native O2 train readout with repeat control.\n- [x] Preserve raw outputs and evidence hashes.\n- [ ] No trainable implementation/test, admission receipt, sync, or dispatch until all six hard gates pass.\n\n## 7. Risk Assessment\nThese are 16-scene bounded observational counterfactuals, not efficacy estimates or training profiles. O1 could mask a referent-defining word; O2 is a global distribution shift. A one-off O1 validation increase of 0.00352 for last-token masking cannot justify choosing that intervention; the train split declined.\n\n## 8. Smell Check\nMask-token choice, feature subsets, fusion weights or thresholds chosen after these readouts would be tuning-only. No renamed counterfactual/gating successor is admitted.\n\nStatus: NO ADMISSION. Bounded executable O1/O2 routes exhausted this cycle, not global scientific exhaustion.\n\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
